<!-- Teaching layer over exact approved source fb8354e. -->
<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">Search results for an old query arrive after the new query has already succeeded. Debouncing can reduce calls, but it cannot decide which completion still owns the screen—or when the server will admit another request.</p>

<!-- @before 1. Client-Side Throttling (Coroutines & Flow) :: animation -->
### Keep pacing, result ownership and admission separate

<section class="pb-figure" data-pb-flow="scene" aria-label="The late search callback is still stale">
